# Temple of Power: "{2}{R}, {T}: Transform this land. Activate only if red sources you controlled dealt 4 or more
# noncombat damage this turn and only as a sorcery." Bot1 cast Ojer Axonil on turn 1 (Mox Ruby, Mountain, Mox Pearl, Mox Jet); Bot2 cast Ornithopter and killed it on
# turn 2 with two Lightning Bolts, and it came back tapped and transformed as Temple of Power (CR 712.14a).
# Turn 3: Black Lotus for {R}{R}{R}. Lightning Bolt deals 3 to Bot2 - three is not four, so the Temple is refused with
# mana to pay for it. Firebolt deals 2 to Bot2's Ornithopter: damage to a creature counts, and two red sources add up (the
# ruling), 5 in all. In the beginning of combat step it is still refused (CR 602.5d: only as a sorcery); in the second main
# phase it transforms, paid with the three Moxen, back into Ojer Axonil, still tapped (CR 701.27c: the same permanent).

